ly the requested structured JSON. Do not include reasoning traces.\n",
      "user_prompt": "QUESTION\nWhy must the fire extinguisher system be tested in test mode?\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE\n\nBEGIN E1\nsource: 992.2 Technical Manual.pdf\nsource_sha256: 35bb8384deb93537b2c99dfa9fe43681b1daa3d7fa7ddb62cbf71be268776456\npages: 9\nsection: [3] Fire extinguisher system [FIRE]\nclause: not specified\ntarget_facets: general\nmetadata: {\"authority\": \"manufacturer_document\", \"document_type\": \"technical_manual\", \"vehicle_generation\": \"992.2\"}\nevidence:\nActivating and testing the Fire extinguisher system.\n\nNOTICE! The system must be tested in test mode to prevent the fire extinguisher from being activated unintentionally, see Testing/activating the system on page 743 .\nEND E1\n\nBEGIN E2\nsource: 992.2 Technical Manual.pdf\nsource_sha256: 35bb8384deb93537b2c99dfa9fe43681b1daa3d7fa7ddb62cbf71be268776456\npages: 741\nsection: Exterior\nclause: not specified\ntarget_facets: general\nmetadata: {\"authority\": \"manufacturer_document\", \"document_type\": \"technical_manual\", \"vehicle_generation\": \"992.2\"}\nevidence:\nThe exterior actuation element is located on the left-hand and right-hand side below the windscreen. Actuating the fire extinguisher system also interrupts the car's electric system.\n\n[2]\n\nEmergency switch + fire extinguisher system.\n\nPull pin.\n\n\u2192 Main switch OFF and fire extinguisher system ON\n\nOn all Porsche 911 Cup (992 II) , the fire extinguisher switches installed in the plenum panel cover must be checked for function and ease of movement before every use of the car.\n\nThe function of the fire extinguisher switch must be tested in test mode of the fire extin -guisher in order to not deploy the extinguisher. When pressing the switch, the electrical system of the car will be shut down as well (FIA requirement). This function must be checked accordingly.\n\n\u2192 In case the switch needs excessive force to be pressed or is not functioning at all, it must be exchanged immediately\nEND E2\n\nBEGIN E3\nsource: 992.2 Technical Manual.pdf\nsource_sha256: 35bb8384deb93537b2c99dfa9fe43681b1daa3d7fa7ddb62cbf71be268776456\npages: 743\nsection: TESTING THE SYSTEM\nclause: not specified\ntarget_facets: general\nmetadata: {\"authority\": \"manufacturer_document\", \"document_type\": \"technical_manual\", \"vehicle_generation\": \"992.2\"}\nevidence:\nPull the switch and set it to its bottom position TEST .\n\nActuate the fire extinguisher system.\n\nSee Actuation outside the car on page 695 .\n\nSee Actuation inside the car on page 694 .\n\n\u2192 LED lights up orange for 10 seconds: Test was successful.\n\n\u2192 LED flashes orange for 10 seconds or longer: Test was not successful.\n\nCheck the possible causes: Battery low, electric fault.\nEND E3\n\nAnswer the question using the required JSON schema.",
