    "answer": "The fire extinguisher system must be tested in test mode to prevent the unintentional activation and deployment of the extinguisher [E1, E2].\n\nTesting in test mode allows the operator to verify the function of the switch and ensure it does not deploy the extinguisher while simultaneously checking that the electrical system shuts down as required by FIA regulations [E2].\n\nTo perform a test, the operator must pull the switch and set it to its bottom position labeled TEST before actuating the system [E3].\n\nA successful test is indicated by an orange LED light that remains lit for 10 seconds, whereas a flashing orange LED indicates a failure such as low battery or an electric fault [E3].",
